  s0 --> s1: an operator edits one node's config file
  s1 --> s2: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s2 --> s3: you send a message
  s3 --> s4: the gateway puts the input into shared custody
  s4 --> s5: the input is handed to the node that owns the channel
  s5 --> s5: a node reads the owner row again
  s5 --> s6: the home's worker claims the input
  s6 --> s7: the input begins in a session of the current generation
  s7 --> s8: the designated node stops
  s8 --> s8: the designated node's heartbeat expires
  s8 --> s9: the gateway moves the channel off the offline home and reserves a notice
